    "Start at M1 Vieux-Port, walk Le Panier and La Major once, cross to Fort Saint-Jean and Mucem, then use bus 60 or the Metro for the return. Start at M1 Vieux-Port.…": "",
    "Start at M1 Vieux-Port, walk Le Panier and La Major once, cross to Fort Saint-Jean and Mucem, then use bus 60 or the Metro for the return.": "",
    "Combine Vieux-Port, selected Panier lanes, La Major and Mucem. Add Notre-Dame de la Garde only by shortening the museum block; keep the Calanques and Cassis for separate days.": "",
    "Check Mucem’s live opening and footbridge status, RTM lines 49/55/60, temporary port or event restrictions, and the route back to the hotel.": "",
    "reviewed 12 October 2026": "",
    "Vieux-Port and Le Panier": "",
    "Keep the walk north of the Old Port: fish market and Hôtel de Ville side, selected public Panier lanes, then Vieille Charité or La Major. Choose this shorter street-and-history version when museum interiors are not the priority.": "",
    "Fort Saint-Jean and Mucem": "",
    "Cross from the Panier side to the fort and Mucem, then give the exhibitions one substantial block. The outdoor fort and harbor views can be a shorter visit; check which spaces and bridges are open.": "",
    "South-bank finish": "",
    "After the north-bank loop, take bus 60 to Notre-Dame de la Garde or stay on the south quays around Saint-Victor. The hill basilica adds its own exposed climb/transfer and should replace, not be squeezed into, a full museum visit.": "",
    "THREE WALKING ZONES": "",
    "Cross the harbor once, then choose a finish.": "",
    "The Old Port is the hinge between a compact north-bank history walk and a separate south-bank hill. Use the quay and transit line as the boundary; the steep lanes are not a flat waterfront stroll.": "",
    "South quay · M1 Vieux-Port": "",
    "Start at the Ombrière or the market-side quay. Bus 49 links this area with Saint-Charles; the Metro is the predictable city return, subject to live RTM service.": "",
    "North bank · Hôtel de Ville to Le Panier": "",
    "Walk the public waterfront past Hôtel de Ville, then choose Vieille Charité or selected lanes toward Place des Moulins. Bus 55/49 can shorten the approach; check the precise stop rather than treating the district as level.": "",
    "La Major · Fort Saint-Jean · J4": "",
    "Continue by the cathedral waterfront to Fort Saint-Jean and Mucem J4. The footbridge links the sites when open. Bus 60 connects the Old Port with Mucem and Notre-Dame de la Garde, allowing a shorter return or a different final stop.": "",
    "Orient at M1 Vieux-Port": "",
    "Choose the north-bank side of the harbor and note the M1 entrance and bus 60 stop before setting off. Keep clear of the fish market and vessel boarding quays.": "",
    "Walk the civic edge into Le Panier": "",
    "Pass Hôtel de Ville, climb only the public lanes you intend to use, then make Vieille Charité or Place des Moulins the turn point. Do not add both a deep lane maze and a timed museum entry.": "",
    "Continue by La Major to the fort and Mucem": "",
    "Use the cathedral-side waterfront to reach Fort Saint-Jean, then the signed footbridge to Mucem J4 if open. Pick one exhibition block; the ticket and current access notice decide the interior sequence.": "",
    "Close by the water, not by retracing the hill": "",
    "Return along the J4/harbor edge and use bus 60, M2 Joliette or the M1 after checking the actual stop and service. If you chose Notre-Dame de la Garde, ride there as the final block and protect the bus 60 return.": "",
    "Marseille Tourism — bus lines 49, 55 and 60": "",
    "RTM — live urban transit maps and service": "",
    "If Fort Saint-Jean or the footbridge closes, keep the north side to Vieille Charité, La Major and the waterfront; take bus 60 to Notre-Dame de la Garde only if service and hill access remain open. In wind, follow staff limits on exposed links.": "",
    "Reach Luminy by RTM B1, check the fire-access gate and Sugiton reservation, then choose the lookout, steep cove descent or a licensed boat. For the Marseille-side…": "",
    "Reach Luminy by RTM B1, check the fire-access gate and Sugiton reservation, then choose the lookout, steep cove descent or a licensed boat.": "",
    "How long is the Sugiton walk?": "",
    "The National Park lists about 30 minutes from Luminy to the belvedere and around 45 minutes to the cove. From the cove, it says to allow at least an hour for the steep return climb. Add your bus, breaks and day conditions; these segments are not a guaranteed round-trip time.": "",
    "Does Sugiton need a reservation in 2027?": "",
    "The 2026 notice listed free advance reservations for specific summer and weekend dates. Those dates are past; the 2027 period and rule are not claimed here. Recheck the National Park’s live Sugiton notice before fixing a date.": "",
    "Can a cruise replace a closed trail?": "",
    "It can be a separate sea excursion only if the operator is sailing. Marseille Tourism says regular cruises do not drop passengers in the coves, and a boat departure does not reopen closed land trails.": "",
    "Luminy to the Sugiton lookout or cove": "",
    "Take B1 toward Luminy–PN des Calanques. The lookout is about 25–30 minutes each way from the trail start; the cove adds a steep descent and a harder climb back. A lookout-only day is a real alternative, not a failed hike.": "",
    "One licensed boat departure": "",
    "Choose a current operator from the Old Port, Cassis or La Ciotat and read the named circuit. Marseille Tourism says regular cruises do not drop passengers ashore in the coves; sea conditions can cancel the trip.": "",
    "Park-free city or shore day": "",
    "When a fire notice closes the massif, stay on an authorized urban route: the Mucem/Fort/Panier loop or a supervised city beach with current access. Do not drive or walk to a barrier and improvise.": "",
    "Pair one access mode with a simple meal back in Marseille. Keep Cassis town, a second trail and the full Mucem visit for other days.": "",
    "THREE ACCESS GATES": "",
    "A map of the massif is not a single entrance.": "",
    "Decide whether you want the Luminy lookout, a difficult cove descent, or a sea view from a vessel. Each starts at a different legal gate and has its own return.": "",
    "Luminy · Sugiton lookout": "",
    "B1 from Avenue du Prado near Place Castellane reaches Luminy–PN des Calanques. The park estimates about 30 minutes on foot to the belvedere; this is the shorter signed out-and-back, still subject to daily closures.": "",
    "Luminy · Sugiton cove": "",
    "The National Park estimates around 45 minutes to reach the cove and warns the steep climb back takes at least an hour. Slippery rocks, heat and crowding can make the descent unsuitable; reaching the lookout is a valid turn-around.": "",
    "Old Port · licensed boat": "",
    "Marseille excursions depart from named Old Port quays; Cassis and La Ciotat have separate port operators. A cruise is a water-view product, not a drop-off at Port-Pin or En-Vau. Sea conditions and operator terms control departure.": "",
    "Check the National Park’s live fire closure and reservation notice, RTM B1 stop/service, heat and wind forecast, and the named licensed boat operator on the morning of travel. The 2027 reservation calendar is not stated as of 12 October 2026.": "",
    "Check the gate before committing": "",
    "Open the National Park’s same-day fire notice and, for Sugiton, the current booking rule. A 2026 notice required free advance reservations on its dated summer/weekend windows; by this review those dates have elapsed and 2027 dates are not published here.": "",
    "Take B1 to Luminy–PN des Calanques": "",
    "Board on Avenue du Prado by Place Castellane, then follow park signs. Carry water, food, walking shoes, a map and sun protection; there is no dependable trail-side refill.": "",
    "Choose the lookout or the cove at the pass": "",
    "The official park estimate is around 30 minutes to the belvedere and 45 to the cove; the steep return from the cove takes at least an hour. Turn back at the viewpoint if heat, footing or time no longer supports the descent.": "",
    "Return by the same gate and earlier bus": "",
    "Protect a margin for the climb, pauses and RTM service. A boat is a separate booked trip: check sea status, and do not plan to disembark in a cove unless the operator and park explicitly authorize that specific activity.": "",
    "Calanques National Park — Sugiton walk and Luminy access": "",
